    "long_instructions": "##Refine Your Schema with AI\r\n\r\nYou’ll now work with AI  to improve your schema from the last level.\r\n\r\n1.\tStart by describing your app idea (for example, Food Allergy Tracker or Medication Reminder) and share your current list of fields and data types by uploading your schema from the previous level.\r\n2.\tAsk the AI to:\r\n\t- Suggest clearer field names or combine similar ones.\r\n\t- Identify fields that could contain sensitive or personal data.\r\n\t- Recommend which fields are safe to show publicly versus privately.\r\n3.\tDecide for yourself which AI suggestions to accept or reject. You can go back to Level 1 to implement these changes and update your schema before moving on to Level 3.\r\n\r\n**Remember:**\r\n- Do not share real personal or health data—use fake names or examples.\r\n- The AI is a thinking partner, not a decision-maker.\r\n- Your goal is a schema that’s clear, organized, and privacy-aware.",
